# TODO: black-brown coalition


@popular_front_coalition
title: A new "Popular Front" coalition?
subtitle: RSDRP + RKP + PSR + [+ musavat_name +]  [? if sapd_formed: + SAPD ?]([+ popular_front_coalition +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: RSDRP + RKP + PSR + [+ musavat_name +] [? if sapd_formed: + SAPD ?]([+ popular_front_coalition +]%) - [? if ((rkp_relation < 65 and rkp_party_leader == "Thälmann") or (rkp_relation < 45 and rkp_party_leader == "Conciliators")): We do not have good enough relations with the RKP. ?][? if (psr_relation < 45 and psr_party_leader == "Joos") or (psr_relation < 65 and psr_party_leader != "Joos" and rkp_party_leader != "Conciliators") or (psr_relation < 55 and psr_party_leader != "Joos" and rkp_party_leader == "Conciliators"): We do not have good enough relations with the PSR. ?][? if communist_coalition < 3 : The Communists are unwilling to compromise at all. ?]
view-if: popular_front_coalition >= 50
choose-if: (((rkp_relation >= 65 and rkp_party_leader == "Thälmann") or (rkp_relation >= 45 and rkp_party_leader == "Conciliators")) and ((psr_relation >= 45 and psr_party_leader == "Joos") or (psr_relation >= 65 and psr_party_leader != "Joos" and rkp_party_leader != "Conciliators") or (psr_relation >= 55 and psr_party_leader != "Joos" and rkp_party_leader == "Conciliators")) and musavat_relation >= 50 and communist_coalition >= 3) or (psr_party_leader == "Joos" and rkp_party_leader == "Conciliators" and psr_relation >= 30 and rkp_relation >= 30)

Could we really form a coalition that included both the Center and the Communists? It seems like an absurd concept, but given our good relationships with both sides, it is not an impossibility.

The far-right might attempt a coup, if such a coalition were formed.

- @popular_front_2: Form the Popular Front!
- @great_popular_front: Form the Popular Front!

@popular_front_2
view-if: psr_party_leader != "Joos" or rkp_party_leader != "Conciliators"

Somehow, both the Communists and Center are at the very least willing to entertain negotiations. Of course, RKP radicals and Center conservatives derail the negotiations almost immediately. The RKP demands leadership of the coalition for themselves and their chairman Ernst Thälmann, [? if rsdrp_r > rkp_r : despite our higher vote share, ?]while the Center is offended by the prospect of helping Bolsheviks enter government. *Something* must be done to restore balance.

- @popular_front_resources
- @popular_front_democracy
- @popular_front_braun
- @coalition_menu: This is impossible. Try another governing arrangement.

@popular_front_resources
title: Use our resources to smooth things over.
unavailable-subtitle: Required: 4 resources
subtitle: -4 resources
choose-if: resources >= 4
on-arrival: resources -= 4
go-to: popular_front_success

@popular_front_democracy
title: Convince the RKP to accept democracy.
subtitle: [? if rkp_party_leader == "Conciliators" : The Conciliator leadership of the RKP at least claim to support the Popular Front. ?]
unavailable-subtitle: Our relationship with the RKP is not high enough.
choose-if: (rkp_relation >= 60 and communist_coalition >= 3) or rkp_party_leader == "Conciliators"
go-to: popular_front_success

@popular_front_braun
title: Use pressure from President Braun to force the parties to cooperate.
view-if: president == "Braun"
go-to: popular_front_success

@great_popular_front
view-if: psr_party_leader == "Joos" and rkp_party_leader == "Conciliators"
on-arrival: rsdrp_in_government = 1; in_popular_front = 1; chancellor = "Breitscheid"; chancellor_party = "RSDRP"; rkp_relation += 10; coup_progress += 2; in_left_front = 0; in_trudovaya_coalition = 0; in_vremennyy_coalition = 0; coalition_dissent = 0;
achievement: grosse_volksfront
go-to: popular_front_civil_war if coup_progress >= 10; popular_front_no_civil_war if coup_progress < 10

Somehow, the coalition is successfully formed! The conciliatory leadership of the Center Party and RKP helped make the negotiations possible. We still need a chancellor; the only acceptable choice among the parties was Rudolf Breitscheid of the RSDRP, acceptable to the Center and RKP [? if president == "Hindenburg" : as well as President Hindenburg, albeit extremely reluctantly ?].

@popular_front_success
on-arrival: rsdrp_in_government = 1; in_popular_front = 1; chancellor = "Breitscheid"; chancellor_party = "RSDRP"; rkp_relation += 10; coup_progress += 2; in_left_front = 0; in_trudovaya_coalition = 0; in_vremennyy_coalition = 0; coalition_dissent = 0;
go-to: popular_front_civil_war if coup_progress >= 10; popular_front_no_civil_war if coup_progress < 10
achievement: volksfront

Somehow, surprisingly, the coalition is successfully formed! We still need a chancellor; the only acceptable choice among the parties was Rudolf Breitscheid of the RSDRP, acceptable to the Center and RKP [? if president == "Hindenburg" : as well as President Hindenburg, albeit extremely reluctantly ?].

@popular_front_no_civil_war
on-arrival: rkp_goals_seen = 0; finance_minister_party = "PSR"; interior_minister_party = "PSR"; economic_minister_party = "PSR"; labor_minister_party = "PSR"; foreign_minister_party = "PSR"; agriculture_minister_party = "PSR"; reichswehr_minister = "I"; leverage = rsdrp_r + rkp_r;
achievement: volksfront

In response to the RKP's entrance into the government, the right-wing takes a "wait-and-see" approach for now. They expect that the Popular Front government will be unstable and incompetent, and will collapse of its own accord, discrediting the left and center and eventually enabling the destruction of the Trudovaya Republic. Our task is to prove them wrong.

The RKP has taken an abstentionist position with regards to ministries. They claim to be participating as the "loyal opposition" within the Popular Front government, supporting us from the outside while also running their own propaganda campaigns to turn workers to their side. They seem to expect that the Popular Front would inevitably fail, and that our failure would benefit them.

- @ministries: First, we must select our ministries.


@popular_front_civil_war
on-arrival: rkp_relation = 80; reichswehr_loyalty += 0.25;

In response to the RKP's entrance into the government, the right-wing immediately launches a coup attempt. Troops of the Stahlhelm and Nazi SA enter Berlin and immediately begin clashing with our supporters! Reactionary officers within the Reichswehr have taken their troops out of the barracks and joined them with the Stahlhelm to stop us from taking power.

The Center manages to diffuse some of the hostility from the Reichswehr and the Stahlhelm, but fail to prevent the outbreak of fighting. We are forced to fight on the same side as the RKP, whether we want to or not.

- @civil_war: A civil war, then.



@far_right_coalition
title: Far-right coalition
subtitle: NTS + VS ([+ far_right_coalition +]%)
view-if: far_right_coalition >= 50
go-to: far_right_win if (year >= 1932 or nts_r >= 44) and president != "Braun"; far_right_fail if (year < 1932 and nts_r < 44) and president != "Braun"; far_right_braun if president == "Braun"
priority: 2

There are enough votes for the Nazis and the VS to form a coalition. [+ nts_leader +] has made his participation in government contingent on being appointed chancellor. It is up to President [+ president +] to decide.

@far_right_win
on-arrival: chancellor = nts_leader; chancellor_party = "NTS"

[? if president == "Hindenburg" : President Hindenburg's camarilla ?][? if president == "Braun" : President Braun somehow ?] has decided that [+ nts_leader +] must be chancellor [? if president == "Hindenburg": , and the aging president accepts their recommendations. ?][? if president == "Braun" : because it is what the constitution would stipulate. ?]

- @hitler_takes_power: What do we do now?


@far_right_fail
on-arrival: chancellor = "Schleicher"; chancellor_party = "I"; pro_republic -= 10; next_election_time = time+5; next_election_month = month + 5; next_election_year = year; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12;

The reactionary establishment is still very skeptical of the Nazis, so instead, [+ president +] appoints Kurt von Schleicher, a former general, as chancellor, to try to "tame" the Nazis.

Schleicher's government is deeply unpopular among all parties of the Reichstag. Despite his support for a coalition with the NTS, the Nazis want power all to themselves, without Schleicher.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@far_right_braun
on-arrival: coup_progress += 2

President Braun faces a dilemma. Is it "democratic" to let democracy be destroyed, if the majority of voters have willed it so? Some, even on the left, suggest that the Nazis would not *truly* be as horrific as their platform suggests, and that giving them power would let them discredit themselves in the eyes of the public.

Alternatively, Braun could use the emergency powers of the presidency. Article 48 has been used by Hindenburg to promulgate anti-democratic and anti-worker policies; can Article 48 be used for good as well as evil?

- @emergency_braun: We will form an emergency government with Braun's support.
- @new_elections: We will have new elections.
- @far_right_win: Let the Nazis form their government.


@left_coalition
title: Is a United Left coalition possible?
subtitle: RSDRP + RKP [? if sapd_formed: + SAPD ?] ([+ left_coalition +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: RSDRP + RKP [? if sapd_formed: + SAPD ?] ([+ left_coalition +]%). [? if rkp_relation < 50 : We do not have adequate relations with the RKP. ?][? if communist_coalition < 3 : The Communists are too committed to their radical ways to partake in government. ?]
view-if: left_coalition >= 50
choose-if: (rkp_relation >= 50 or (rkp_party_leader == "Conciliators" and rkp_relation >= 40)) and communist_coalition >= 3

There are enough votes for a RSDRP + RKP coalition government, if such a thing were actually possible.

The far-right might attempt a coup, if such a coalition were formed.

- @left_coalition_impossible: This is impossible.
- @left_coalition_possible: This could be possible.

@left_coalition_impossible
go-to: coalition_menu

A far left coalition is impossible.


@left_coalition_possible

The RKP is still very reluctant to join a coalition, despite grassroots friendliness between our memberships. The Stalinist leadership is vehemently against such a thing. They demand the appointment of Ernst Thälmann as chancellor in exchange for a coalition. [? if president == "Hindenburg" : There is no chance whatsoever that President Hindenburg would approve of the appointment of a die-hard communist as chancellor. ?] Alternatively, if our relations with them are good enough, we could convince them to support the appointment of one of our centrist or left-leaning members as chancellor.

- @thalmann_chancellor: Appoint Thälmann as chancellor.
- @left_coalition_resources
- @left_coalition_relations
- @coalition_menu: Try a different governing arrangement.

@thalmann_chancellor
choose-if: president == "Braun" and reformist_strength + neorevisionist_strength < left_strength
unavailable-subtitle: [? if president != "Braun": President [+ president +] would never allow such a thing. ?] [? if reformist_strength >= left_strength : Most in the parliamentary party would not support Thälmann as chancellor. ?]
on-arrival: chancellor = "Thälmann"; chancellor_party = "RKP"; rkp_relation = 80; in_left_front = 1; rsdrp_in_government = 1 

With great reluctance, President [+ president +] appoints [+ chancellor +] as chancellor.

Immediately, [+ chancellor +] goes to work building a "Soviet Germany": consolidating as much power as possible in the RKP, purging state institutions of anti-communists, and sending street fighters against the "enemies of the people".

In response to [+ chancellor +] being appointed Chancellor, the right-wing forces launches almost immediately launch an attempted coup. Troops of the Stahlhelm and Nazi SA enter Berlin and immediately begin clashing with our supporters! Reactionary officers within the Reichswehr have taken their troops out of the barracks and joined them with the Stahlhelm to stop the RKP from taking power. We are forced to be on the same side as the RKP, whether we want to or not.

- @civil_war


@left_coalition_resources
