There are enough votes to form a majority coalition consisting of the RSDRP, Center (Z), Bavarian People's (BVP), Democratic ([+ musavat_name +]), and People's (K-D) parties. Given our rather weak electoral performance, [? if rsdrp_no_confidence = 1 : and our previous vote of no confidence against the government, ?][? if no_confidence_against_rsdrp = 1 : and the vote of no confidence against us, ?] President Kornilov has asked the Center Party to take the lead role in forming a government.

# TODO: if the RSDRP participated in bringing down the previous government via a vote-of-no-confidence, or if we were essentially removed from government by our coalition partners, we should be more reluctant to participate in a new government.

@vremennyy_coalition_psr_lead_2

The Center chancellor is likely to be Doctor Andrei Shingarev of the Kadet Party [? if chancellor = "Brüning" : again. ?][? if chancellor != "Brüning": . ?] He is known for his conservatism and sympathy for nationalism, being on the right wing of the Kadets. [? if austerity >= 2 : Due to the government's austerity policies, many of our members are reluctant to participate in this coalition again. Some support a "toleration" arrangement in which we will provide outside support to prevent the far-right from either entering government or calling a successful no-confidence vote. Others support entering into pure opposition, and letting the right do what it wishes. ?]

Brüning is not opposed to a coalition with us. Alternatively, we could enter a "toleration" agreement.

- @join_bruning: Join the Brüning coalition.
- @bruning_oppo: Join the opposition.
- @toleration_bruning: We will "tolerate" a minority Brüning government.
- @unity_government

@join_bruning
view-if: vremennyy_coalition >= 50 or neo_trudovaya_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: rsdrp_in_government = 1; rsdrp_toleration = 0; in_vremennyy_coalition = 1; chancellor = "Brüning"; chancellor_party = "PSR"; foreign_minister_party = "K-D"; interior_minister_party = "PSR"; justice_minister_party = "PSR"; labor_minister_party = "PSR"; reichswehr_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = "PSR"; finance_minister_party = "PSR"; agriculture_minister_party = "PSR"; leverage = 25 if leverage >= 25;
go-to: ministries

Heinrich Brüning welcomes us into his new cabinet. Now, we have our pick of ministries.

@bruning_oppo
on-arrival: rsdrp_in_government = 0; rsdrp_toleration = 0; chancellor = "Brüning"; chancellor_party = "PSR"; foreign_minister_party = "K-D"; interior_minister_party = "PSR"; justice_minister_party = "PSR"; labor_minister_party = "PSR"; reichswehr_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = "PSR"; finance_minister_party = "PSR"; agriculture_minister_party = "PSR"; vremennyy_coalition_failed = 1

By refusing to join the vremennyy coalition or tolerating it, we essentially throw the balance of government to the right wing. [? if right_coalition >= 50 : There are enough votes to form a right-wing coalition that includes the VS. However, the VS leader, Hugenberg, is opposed to a coalition with the "November criminals" of the Center Party. And of course, the NTS is not interested in coalition government. This means that there will not be enough votes to form a majority coalition. ?][? if right_coalition < 50 : There are not enough votes to form a right-wing coalition that includes the VS, and they are not interested in joining in a coalition with the "November criminals" of the Center Party, anyhow. And of course, the NTS is not interested in coalition government. This means that there is no route to a majority coalition. ?]

If we do not at least "tolerate" the government, there will be new elections in a few months. In the meantime, the President and Chancellor may use the emergency powers granted by Article 48 of the constitution to essentially govern by decree. And it is not at all clear that we will do any better in the next election.

- @join_bruning: Join the Brüning coalition.
- @toleration_bruning: We will tolerate Brüning after all.
- @brauns_dilemma
- @new_elections: New elections, it is!


